  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing due to **host disk full** on the upload volume \u2014 not app, DB, or permissions.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n- App `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` (E1, E6), DB `incidentlab-db-1` is `running (healthy)` (E1, E7).\n- App `/health` returns `503 unhealthy` (E2).\n- App logs show `POST /upload 500` with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` at `out.write(chunk)` in `/app/main.py line 59 upload` (E4).\n- Same logs show health-check `503` caused by identical `OSError: [Errno 28]` on probe write `open(probe,\"wb\")` in `/app/main.py line 116 health` (E4) \u2014 so unhealthy status is **symptom** of same write failure.\n- DB logs show `database system is ready to accept connections` with no errors (E5) \u2014 rules out DB as cause. DB health is `healthy` (E7).\n- Bind mount is `/srv/lab-data -> /data rw:true` (E6), user `1000:1000` (E6).\n- Filesystem holding `/srv/lab-data` is its own mountpoint `use_percent: 100.0`, `available_mb: 0.0` (E8) \u2014 root cause.\n- Inode use on that filesystem is only `1.7%` (E8) \u2014 rules out inode exhaustion, confirms capacity exhaustion.\n- Root filesystem `/` has `use_percent: 6.8`, `available_mb: 91424.7` (E9) \u2014 rules out system-disk full, isolates to `/srv/lab-data` volume.\n- `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is dir owned `1000:1000 mode 0755`, `app_user_can_write: true` for app `1000:1000` (E10) \u2014 rules out permission/ownership. Mount is writable (E6).\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nRoot cause: `/srv/lab-data` disk full (E8) causing `ENOSPC` on writes (E4). Unhealthy health-check (E2, E4) and `500` uploads (E4) are symptoms. DB healthy (E5, E7, E1), permissions OK (E10), inodes OK (E8), system disk OK (E9).\n",
